This pack gives guidance. It is not a certification, an audit, or legal advice.
It is not affiliated with the Australian Signals Directorate, the Australian
Cyber Security Centre, or any other agency.

ISM text in the snapshots is the ASD catalogue, processed into short chunks
with the control ID, version, date, and a link back to the public manual.
The machine-readable mirror is the public ism-oscal repository. That upstream
repository did not publish a licence file that this pack could record. Do not
treat these chunks as a substitute for the manual on cyber.gov.au.

MITRE ATT&CK technique IDs and names are MITRE's. This pack stores the ID,
the name, and the URL. It does not store the STIX bundle.

Other pages are stored as extracts with the URL and the content hash. If a
fetch fails, the last good extract stays and the failure is recorded in
knowledge/manifest.json.
